# [[.Title]]

[[.Title]] is an [Anetos](https://anetos.dev) application[[if .API]]: a JSON
API under `/api/v1`, with no pages or sessions[[else]]: pages rendered on the
server with templ, sessions and CSRF protection[[end]]. Anetos is a
batteries-included Go web framework: typed, `net/http` underneath, and one
binary that runs the web server, the queue workers, the scheduler and the
listeners. Its version is the one `go.mod` requires (`anetos.dev/anetos`).
[[- if .Web]] [[.KitSentence]][[end]] The database is [[.DBLabel]].

## Read the docs from here

The documentation, at this project's Anetos version, is built into the
tool. Read it before guessing an API:

```sh
go tool anetos docs                        # list the pages
go tool anetos docs queues                 # print one (guides/queues)
go tool anetos docs --search "retry a job" # find pages
```

Pages link to each other as `../guides/mail.md`: that's
`go tool anetos docs guides/mail`. Don't assume another framework's
names or APIs: Anetos's are in the docs and in `go doc anetos.dev/anetos/<package>`.

## Ask the app instead of reading all of it

```sh
go tool anetos model:list   # the models: tables, columns (PostCols…), relations
go run . route:list --json  # every route: its handler, types and middleware
go run . db:schema          # the tables as the database has them (or db:schema <table>)
go run . about              # versions, services, the settings read (secrets hidden)
```

Add `--json` for JSON you can parse. The project's MCP server
(`go tool anetos mcp`, in your MCP settings) has these as tools too:
`docs_search`, `docs_read`, `model_list`, `route_list`, `db_schema`,
`app_about`, `check`, `security_check`.

## Before you call a change done

```sh
go tool anetos check    # generate, build, vet, test, doctor, security; --json for one object
```

It must pass. Fix what it reports, then run it again. Its security step
runs the security check's basic rules: fix a finding as the
`anetos-security` skill says, never by ignoring a problem. In a fresh clone
there is no `.env` (it holds secrets, so it isn't committed): `check`
then checks the project's files without the app's settings, and the
app's own commands (`go run . …`) refuse to start. Make one first with
`cp .env.example .env && go tool anetos key:generate`.

## Commands

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `go tool anetos dev` | Runs the app with live reload on http://localhost:8080[[if .API]]/api/v1[[end]], regenerating code as files change |
| `go run . migrate` | Runs the migrations (`migrate:rollback`, `migrate:status`, `migrate:fresh`, `db:seed` too) |
| `go test ./...` | The tests (`anetostest`: each test gets the app with a migrated database) |
| `go tool anetos generate` | The models' typed columns (`models_gen.go`), after changing a model |
[[- if .API]]
| `go run . openapi` | Updates `openapi.json`, the API's description, after changing a route or its types (a test checks it) |
[[- end]]
[[- if .Web]]
| `go tool templ generate` | The views' Go code (`*_templ.go`), after changing a `.templ` file |
[[- end]]
| `go tool anetos make:crud <Model> <field:type>...` | A model, its migration, [[if .API]]JSON endpoints[[else]]pages[[end]] to list, show, create, edit and delete it, routes and tests (types: `string`, `text`, `email`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `date`; add `:optional` or `:unique`) |
| `go tool anetos make:model <Name> --migration` | A model and its table's migration |
| `go tool anetos make:migration <name>` | A migration (`create_posts_table`, `add_slug_to_posts`) |
| `go tool anetos make:handler <Name>` | A handler |
| `go tool anetos make:middleware <Name>` | A middleware |
| `go tool anetos make:auth` | Accounts: registration, login, email verification, password reset[[if .API]], API tokens, two-factor login[[else]], login with Google or GitHub, account settings, API tokens[[end]] |
[[- if .Web]]
| `go tool anetos make:admin` | The admin interface at `/admin` (after `make:auth`) |
[[- end]]
| `go tool anetos make:agent <Name>` | An AI agent (`ai.Agent`) in the app, with a typed tool |
| `go tool anetos add <module>` | Installs a plugin (`plugins.go` lists them) |
| `go tool anetos doctor` | Checks the project and the app's settings |
| `go tool anetos security:check` | Checks the code, routes, settings and dependencies against security rules (`--level=advanced`, `--format=json`) |
| `go run . route:list` | Every route: method, path, name |
| `go run . help` | The app's commands |
| `go tool anetos build` | One production binary, `bin/[[.Bin]]` |

## Where things go

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `main.go` | `setup`: builds the app's services from the settings (`db.Connect`, `cache.New`…) and registers the routes; `main` runs a command |
| `routes/` | The routes[[if .API]] (`api.go`, under `/api/v1`)[[else]] (`web.go`: the page group with sessions and CSRF)[[end]] |
| `app/handlers/` | Handlers |
| `app/models/` | Models (structs embedding `db.Model`) and their generated `models_gen.go` |
| `database/migrations/` | Migrations (one file each, which adds itself to `All` in `migrations.go`) and seeders |
| `database/factories/` | Model factories, for tests and seeders |
[[- if .Web]]
| `views/` | templ pages and the layout |
[[- if .HasUI]]
| `views/ui/` | The CSS framework's components (`@ui.Button`, `@ui.Field`…): the only place with CSS classes |
[[- end]]
| `public/`, `public/static/` | The web root, and static files served under `/assets` |
[[- end]]
| `locales/` | The messages' translations (`locales/en/app.yaml`) |
| `plugins.go` | The plugins, written by `anetos add` and `anetos remove` |
| `.env` | Settings and secrets (never committed); `.env.example` lists them |

## Conventions

- **Generators first.** Use `make:*` for a new model, resource, migration,
  handler or accounts, then edit what they write: the result builds,
  is tested and follows the conventions below.
- **Handlers are typed.** `web.H(func(c *web.Ctx, in CreatePost) (Post, error))`
  binds and validates the input struct (`validate:"required|max:200"`),
  and returns the output; a plain `func(c *web.Ctx) error` works too.
- **Queries are typed.** Conditions use the generated columns
  (`db.Query[models.Post](ctx).Where(models.PostCols.Title.Eq(t))`), so a
  wrong name doesn't compile. Raw SQL takes `?` placeholders, never
  values built into the string.
- **Services come from the context**: `cache.From(ctx)`, `storage.From(ctx)`,
  `queue.Dispatch(ctx, job)`. `setup` builds them with `New`; a server
  connection is `Connect`.
- **Settings** go in `.env`, named after their area (`DB_`, `CACHE_`,
  `MAIL_`…); the one that picks a backend is `<AREA>_DRIVER`.
- **CRUD names** are `index`, `new`, `create`, `show`, `edit`, `update`,
  `delete`, for route names and handler methods alike.
[[- if and .Web .HasUI]]
- **Pages are built from `views/ui`'s components**: no CSS classes in
  `views/` outside `views/ui`. Forms carry `@view.CSRFField(ctx)`.
[[- else if .Web]]
- **Pages** follow the markup of the existing views. Forms carry
  `@view.CSRFField(ctx)`.
[[- end]]
- **Dependencies:** don't add a router, ORM, validator, session, queue,
  mail or cache library: Anetos has them. Check the docs first.
- **Generated files** (`*_templ.go`, `models_gen.go`, `plugins.go`) are
  never edited by hand: change the source and regenerate.
- **Words**: users log in and log out. Use the names the docs use.
- **Tests** use `anetostest.New(t, setup)` and its request helpers
  ([[if .API]]`app.GetJSON("/api/v1").AssertOK()`[[else]]`app.Get("/").AssertOK()`[[end]]); every change comes with its test.

